    "text": "Skip to lesson\nr\nrecall\nweave\n● PRIVATE · RUNS ON THIS DEVICE\nFIELD NOTES / BIOLOGY 01\nLearn the links,\nnot just the labels.\n\nBuild a mental model of how cells move energy—from sunlight to usable work. Each next prompt is chosen from your learning state, not a fixed quiz order.\n\n↗\n6 short challenges\n·\nabout 4 minutes\n01\nLight energy\n02\nGlucose\n03\nATP\n\nA concept pathway. The selector can revisit a prerequisite when evidence suggests a useful review.\n\nBring your own lesson\n\nChoose a local JSON deck to preview its questions. Nothing is uploaded. The current session changes only when you start the selected deck.\n\nChoose a deck file\nDownload example deck\nUse bundled lesson\n\nUp to 100 questions and 32 concepts. Files stay in this tab’s memory.\n\nREADY TO BEGIN\n0 / 6\nYOUR STARTING POINT\nWhat do you already know?\n\nNo score to protect. Your answers only help choose the next useful connection. You’ll see why each answer is right, then put the idea to work.\n\n✳\nTransparent by design\nThe model shows its assumptions and updates. It is a learning aid, not a diagnosis.\nStart the thread →\nOr inspect a scripted learner simulation ↗\n\nClearly synthetic; compares the adaptive selector with fixed deck order.\n\nSave or resume an unfinished lesson\nKeep or restore a learning trace\nHow the adaptive model works\nRECALLWEAVE · DEMO BUILD\nOriginal demo deck · OpenStax Biology 2e attribution in the wrap-up"
  },
